N00B_DIAG(BACKEND_TARGET_UNAVAILABLE, "N00B-B1000", ERROR,
    "LLVM cannot generate code for this machine",
    "The LLVM libraries this toolchain was built with do not include a code\n"
    "generator for the machine n00b is running on, so no program can be\n"
    "built. Install a toolchain built for this machine, or point\n"
    "N00B_TOOLCHAIN at one.")
N00B_DIAG(BACKEND_TARGET_CPU, "N00B-B1001", ERROR,
    "LLVM cannot generate code for the selected CPU",
    "n00b asks LLVM to tune code for a CPU: this machine's CPU by default on\n"
    "macOS and with --native, the baseline CPU with --generic. LLVM rejected\n"
    "the CPU or its feature list. Build with --generic to use the baseline\n"
    "CPU for the target.")
N00B_DIAG(BACKEND_OBJECT_EMISSION, "N00B-B1002", ERROR,
    "LLVM could not write machine code for a module",
    "LLVM failed while writing the object code for one module of the\n"
    "program. The message includes LLVM's own explanation. This usually\n"
    "means the machine ran out of memory or the generated code exceeds a\n"
    "limit of the target, such as the size of a single function.")
N00B_DIAG(INLINE_FUNCTION_RECURSIVE, "N00B-B1004", ERROR,
    "an `inline` function calls itself, directly or through other functions",
    "An `inline` function is copied into every caller, so it cannot reach a\n"
    "call to itself: the copy would never end. Remove `inline`, or move the\n"
    "recursive part into a separate function that is not inline.")
N00B_DIAG(INLINE_FUNCTION_INDIRECT_CALL, "N00B-B1005", ERROR,
    "an `inline` function calls through a function value",
    "n00b checks that an `inline` function never reaches a call to itself.\n"
    "A call through a callback or function value could lead anywhere, so\n"
    "it cannot be checked. Call a named function instead, or remove\n"
    "`inline`.")
N00B_DIAG(INLINE_FUNCTION_AS_VALUE, "N00B-B1006", ERROR,
    "an `inline` function is used as a function value",
    "An `inline` function has no address of its own: it exists only as\n"
    "copies inside its callers, so it cannot be stored, passed or returned\n"
    "as a value. Remove `inline` to use the function as a value.")
N00B_DIAG(BACKEND_LLVM_WARNING, "N00B-B1003", WARNING,
    "LLVM reported a problem while optimizing the whole program",
    "With --lto, n00b links every module and the runtime into one LLVM\n"
    "module before optimizing it. LLVM reported something unexpected while\n"
    "doing so; the program was still built. The message is LLVM's own.")
